  "notes": "Official cause code was not provided in FORM-366 FIELDS (TBD/provisional) despite a clear narrative root cause (debris in relief valve seat from improper manual venting practice); per rules, cause_code/category copied verbatim as TBD/provisional. The system EK generically covers both DG trains; 'B' train DG modeled as a separate System node since narrative explicitly states it remained capable of performing its specified safety function throughout the period (stated-operable backup). KC (Demineralized Water) system mentioned only in design-context passage about make-up water not being creditable during a DBA -- not modeled per rule 6, as it is design context. Previous similar event (2014) captured as stub LER per rule 9; no LER number given in narrative, so key set to a description-derived placeholder since no formal number was stated (report says only 'documented in the plant's corrective action program')."
